Hello,

Ran a quick search for this and didn't see anything so I am posting;
if I did miss something, please accept my apologies and disregard.

Situation:
Playing in Sokoban in Unnethack, on the first level. The level has the
room with the down staircase and the boulders in sort of a diamond
formation on the right, and the room with the up staircase on the
left, with a hallway of boulders underneath. What separates the up-
staircase room from the down-staircase room is a "wall" of iron bars
rather than a solid wall.

I go about trying to solve the puzzle, when suddenly I notice several
boulders have been turned to rocks--definitely not by my own doing. I
discover a centaur spawned on the up-staircase side and is shooting a
wand of striking through the bars--that's what destroyed the boulders.
Although I was able to deal with him before he destroyed more
boulders, he had started shooting even before I could see him
(boulders blocked my LOS, so I didn't see him myself till I was close
to the wall of bars) so I lost several useful boulders. Might be able
to still complete the level without crazy tricks, but not sure.

I have no idea whether this was intentional or not--I guess even in
vanilla Nethack something could spawn with a wand of striking and use
it to destroy boulders on you, but the level designs were smaller and
more crowded, with no iron bars, so it seemed much less likely to
cause major damage. And I know Sokoban in Unnethack was made to be
more challenging in general so maybe that was indeed the point--and if
so, please disregard.

But if it was not intended, I thought I'd point it out in case its of
use to anyone.  Unnethack's Sokoban level designs makes this a
particular issue. (I did not find any way to contact the developer
directly.)

For the record I was playing in version 3.6.0 -- didn't notice 4.0 was
out till I started looking things up, but I didn't see anything in the
changelog that suggested the situation would be different in the newer
version.

